Policy improvement step
Assume that we were able to find a new policy \(\Pi_{n+1}\) such that
\[
\begin{aligned}
r_{d_{n+1}} + \gamma P_{d_{n+1}}v_n & \ge r_{d_n} + \gamma P_{d_n}v_n \\
\implies r_{d_{n+1}} & \ge [I - \gamma P_{d_{n+1}}]v_n \quad \text{(call this equation 1)}
\end{aligned}
\]
Now, based on the new policy \(\Pi_{n+1}\), we can find
\[
v_{n+1} = r_{d_{n+1}} + \gamma P_{d_{n+1}}v_{n+1} \quad \text{(call this equation 2)}
\]
We are going to show that \(v_{n+1} \ge v_n\), that is, for all the states the newly chosen policy \(\Pi_{n+1}\) gives a value at least as high as the previous policy \(\Pi_n\).
